---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const LIVE = "deploy/live/live_runs.py";

const H = {
  short: "What's tested on real clouds and at full size",
  how: "Live cloud tests, and the record that gates a release",
  rules: "What makes a cloud due, and the nightly load tests",
  ref: "Targets, workflows and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      The live tests deploy Iki to a real Google Cloud project or AWS account, check it, and tear it
      all down: an hour or two, and a few dollars, each. So they never run in CI. Each passing run
      is recorded in the repository, <code>make live-due</code> says which cloud's last passing run
      is behind what it tests, and a release tag refuses to build until every cloud has passed at an
      ancestor of it with nothing it tests changed since. Imports, the grid, the queue and files are
      load-tested every night (<Adr n={[97, 103, 107]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <p>
      <code>make check-gcp-live</code> and <code>make check-aws-live</code> run the live suites
      with the project or role they're given, which is billed (<Path
        p="deploy/gcp/tests/test_gcp_live.py"
      />, <Path p="deploy/aws/tests/test_aws_live.py" />). A passing run of a clean tree appends an
      entry to <Path p="deploy/live-runs.json" />: the cloud, the commit, when it began, how long it
      took, its cost at list prices, the suite's version and the checks that passed. Nothing about
      the account it ran in. A failed run, or one of a tree with changes, records nothing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>make live-due</code> prints each cloud's last passing run and the relevant paths that
      changed since (<Path p={LIVE} sym="def due(" />). The publish and release workflows both start
      with the gate: for a tag, every cloud needs a passing run of a commit the tag descends from,
      with no relevant change between them; any other ref only reports (<Path
        p=".github/workflows/release.yml"
        sym="live_runs.py gate HEAD"
      />, <PageLink to="Releases and images" />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="What makes a cloud's live test due" open>
        <p>
          What every cloud's run tests: the chart, the images and what they're built from, the Wasm
          modules' build scripts and pinned digests, the locked dependencies, the deploy build, the
          plugins it installs, the worker's crates, and the server code the cloud decides. Each
          cloud adds its own directory under <code>deploy/</code> and its own server modules; a test
          fails if a module of the server that's one cloud's isn't listed for it.
        </p>
        <Excerpt file={LIVE} start="^RELEVANT: dict" />
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Nightly scale tests">
        <p>
          A scheduled workflow runs four load tests every night, each building the Wasm modules it
          loads first (<code>make test-wasm</code>): an import of ten million entities, interrupted halfway; the
          grid at ten million rows; 32 workers leasing from 100,000 queued jobs behind a million
          finished; and a project's Files at a million files (<Adr n="0103" />, <Path
            p=".github/workflows/scale.yml"
          />). The grid at a hundred million rows, a 119 GB database, is <code
            >make check-scale-grid</code
          > on a machine with the disk, before a release (<Path p="Makefile" sym="check-scale:" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Targets</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><code>make live-due</code> (<code>STRICT=1</code> exits 1 if any is due), <code>check-gcp-live</code>, <code>check-aws-live</code></li>
        <li><code>make gcp-live-cost</code>, <code>aws-live-cost</code>: what the last run cost</li>
        <li><code>make check-scale</code> and its four parts</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={LIVE} />: the record, <code>due</code> and <code>gate</code></li>
        <li><Path p="deploy/live" />: the shared harness and its check plugin</li>
        <li><PageLink to="Cloud infrastructure" />: what the live tests deploy</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0097" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0103" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0107" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
